  - m_Id: 97608845849575424
    m_Localized: Metallurgy Manual
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 97608911280717824
    m_Localized: 1. Introduction
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 97609007955230720
    m_Localized: Metal Ingots can be smelted inside a Furnace using TWO pieces of either Scrap Metal or Metal Ore. They can have various levels of purity. The higher the purity, the more valuable the ingot will be.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 97609040402366464
    m_Localized: 2. Smelting
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 97609058861498368
    m_Localized: "The purity of an ingot is determined by the materials used to smelt it. Using Scrap Metals will yield a lower purity, while using Metal Ores will yield a higher one. Additionally, Flux Agent can be added to the furnace to improve the purity, Any added agent will be consumed.\n\nThe Furnace requires a source of power. The smelting process happens overnight."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
